| `guest` runs one application inside another in a browser, and this is not
| one. `Load` answers an Exception rather than pretending to have started
| something — on a machine a program hosts another by *linking* it, which is
| a different thing done a different way (`code_abi.h`'s hosting section).
|
| The module is linkable here anyway, so one application can be built both
| ways and ask `Linked` which it is. The half that can actually run a guest
| is a `.a` linked into a `--target wasm` build; nothing in this suite is one.

link "native_modules/guest.so" as guest

emit Load { app = "mail", url = "mail.wasm", into = "#panel" } to guest get r
assert r ∈ Exception
assert r.source = "guest"

emit Unload { app = "mail" } to guest get u
assert u ∈ Exception
assert u.source = "guest"

emit Tell { app = "mail", particle = Ping {} } to guest get t
assert t ∈ Exception
assert t.source = "guest"

| A class it does not handle is null, not an error: the particle may have
| been meant for something else entirely.
emit Whatever {} to guest get other
assert other = null
